{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "c11ec0a3-9b8a-4f3f-bd83-cedt-payment-flow",
		"name": "CEDT Marketplace — Stripe Payment Flow",
		"description": "End-to-end test of the manual-capture destination-charge payment loop.\n\nRun folders **0 through 6** in order with **Collection Runner** — everything cascades via collection variables. **Skip folder 7** in the Runner (those are alternate paths; run them by hand on individual payments).\n\n### Prerequisites\n1. Backend running on `{{baseUrl}}` (default `http://localhost:3003`).\n2. `stripe listen --forward-to {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/stripe --forward-connect-to {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/stripe` running in another terminal.\n3. Seller has already completed Stripe Connect onboarding (`connectStatus = ACTIVE`).\n4. **`stripeSecretKey`** variable filled in with your raw `sk_test_...` value.\n5. Other variables: `sellerEmail`, `sellerPassword`, `buyerEmail`, `buyerPassword`, `categoryId`, `pickupLocationId`.\n\n### Setting `stripeSecretKey`\nThe collection calls Stripe's API directly to confirm the PaymentIntent (Postman can't simulate cards otherwise). Open the collection's **Variables** tab and paste your raw test secret key (from Stripe Dashboard → Developers → API keys → `sk_test_...`) into `stripeSecretKey`. No encoding.\n\n### Running\n- In Postman → Collections → this collection → **Run** → select folders 0–6 → optionally set **Delay between requests** to `500ms` for extra safety → Run.\n- Folder 7 (cancel/refund) is mutually exclusive — pick one and run by hand on a fresh Payment.\n",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "0. Auth",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Login — Seller",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"const token = json.accessToken || json.token;",
									"pm.expect(token, 'access token in response').to.be.a('string');",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('sellerToken', token);",
									"if (json.user && json.user.id) pm.collectionVariables.set('sellerUserId', json.user.id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{sellerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{sellerPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Login — Buyer",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"const token = json.accessToken || json.token;",
									"pm.expect(token, 'access token in response').to.be.a('string');",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('buyerToken', token);",
									"if (json.user && json.user.id) pm.collectionVariables.set('buyerUserId', json.user.id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{buyerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{buyerPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "1. Seller Onboarding",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Start Stripe Connect onboarding",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.expect(json.url, 'onboarding url').to.match(/^https:\\/\\//);",
									"if (json.stripeConnectAccountId) pm.collectionVariables.set('stripeConnectAccountId', json.stripeConnectAccountId);",
									"console.log('Open this URL in a browser to complete onboarding:', json.url);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sellers/onboarding",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["sellers", "onboarding"]
						},
						"description": "Returns a Stripe-hosted URL. Open it in a browser, fill in test data, click Submit. Then run `Refresh seller status` to force-pull state from Stripe."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Refresh seller status from Stripe",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sellers/onboarding/refresh",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["sellers", "onboarding", "refresh"]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "GET /sellers/me",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const p = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('connectStatus = ACTIVE', () => pm.expect(p.connectStatus).to.eql('ACTIVE'));",
									"pm.test('chargesEnabled', () => pm.expect(p.chargesEnabled).to.be.true);",
									"pm.test('payoutsEnabled', () => pm.expect(p.payoutsEnabled).to.be.true);",
									"if (p.stripeConnectAccountId) pm.collectionVariables.set('stripeConnectAccountId', p.stripeConnectAccountId);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sellers/me",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["sellers", "me"]
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "2. Listing & Checkout",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Seller creates listing",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.expect(json.id, 'listing id').to.be.a('string');",
									"pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('AVAILABLE');",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('listingId', json.id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Postman Loop Test\",\n  \"description\": \"Created via Postman collection for end-to-end Stripe test\",\n  \"price\": 75000,\n  \"categoryId\": \"{{categoryId}}\",\n  \"pickupLocationId\": \"{{pickupLocationId}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/listings",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["listings"]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Buyer initiates /checkout",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.expect(json.paymentIntentId, 'paymentIntentId').to.match(/^pi_/);",
									"pm.expect(json.clientSecret).to.be.a('string');",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('paymentIntentId', json.paymentIntentId);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('paymentId', json.paymentId);",
									"console.log('Now run in your shell:');",
									"console.log('  stripe payment_intents confirm ' + json.paymentIntentId + ' --payment-method pm_card_visa');"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{buyerToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"listingId\": \"{{listingId}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/checkout",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["checkout"]
						},
						"description": "The next request confirms the PaymentIntent against Stripe's API directly using your `stripeSecretKey` collection variable, so the Runner can complete end-to-end without dropping to a shell."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Stripe — Confirm PaymentIntent (test mode)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK from Stripe', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const pi = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('PI requires_capture (auth held)', () => pm.expect(pi.status).to.eql('requires_capture'));",
									"// Give the webhook a moment to propagate to the backend before downstream assertions.",
									"const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));",
									"await sleep(2500);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{stripeSecretKey}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{ "key": "payment_method", "value": "pm_card_visa" }
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "https://api.stripe.com/v1/payment_intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/confirm",
							"protocol": "https",
							"host": ["api", "stripe", "com"],
							"path": ["v1", "payment_intents", "{{paymentIntentId}}", "confirm"]
						},
						"description": "Calls Stripe's REST API directly to simulate the buyer paying with `pm_card_visa`. The script then waits 2.5s for the webhook to reach the backend so subsequent verifications see the new state.\n\n**Requires** the `stripeSecretKey` collection variable to be set to your raw `sk_test_...` value (no encoding)."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Verify listing → WAITING_FOR_PAYMENT",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const l = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('listing locked', () => pm.expect(l.status).to.be.oneOf(['WAITING_FOR_PAYMENT', 'PAID']));",
									"pm.test('currentPaymentIntentId set', () => pm.expect(l.currentPaymentIntentId).to.match(/^pi_/));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/listings/{{listingId}}",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["listings", "{{listingId}}"]
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "3. After Card Auth (run stripe confirm in shell first)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Verify listing → PAID",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const l = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('listing PAID after card auth', () => pm.expect(l.status).to.eql('PAID'));",
									"pm.test('buyerId attached', () => pm.expect(l.buyerId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('buyerUserId')));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/listings/{{listingId}}",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["listings", "{{listingId}}"]
						},
						"description": "If this still says WAITING_FOR_PAYMENT, the card-confirm webhook hasn't arrived yet. Check `stripe listen` terminal — you should see `payment_intent.amount_capturable_updated` and `charge.succeeded`."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Verify Payment → REQUIRES_CAPTURE",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const p = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('Payment REQUIRES_CAPTURE', () => pm.expect(p.status).to.eql('REQUIRES_CAPTURE'));",
									"pm.test('stripeChargeId populated', () => pm.expect(p.stripeChargeId).to.match(/^ch_/));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{buyerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/{{paymentId}}",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["payments", "{{paymentId}}"]
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "4. Confirm Receipt & Capture",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Buyer confirms receipt → triggers capture",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('Payment SUCCEEDED', () => pm.expect(json.payment.status).to.eql('SUCCEEDED'));",
									"pm.test('Listing RECEIVED', () => pm.expect(json.listing.status).to.eql('RECEIVED'));",
									"pm.test('capturedAt set', () => pm.expect(json.payment.capturedAt).to.be.a('string'));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{buyerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/listings/{{listingId}}/confirm-received",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["listings", "{{listingId}}", "confirm-received"]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Verify Payment has all Stripe IDs",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const p = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('stripeChargeId', () => pm.expect(p.stripeChargeId).to.match(/^ch_/));",
									"pm.test('stripeTransferId', () => pm.expect(p.stripeTransferId).to.match(/^tr_/));",
									"pm.test('stripeApplicationFeeId', () => pm.expect(p.stripeApplicationFeeId).to.match(/^fee_/));",
									"pm.test('sellerNet == amount - fee', () => pm.expect(p.sellerNetSatang).to.eql(p.amountSatang - p.platformFeeSatang));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{buyerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/{{paymentId}}",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["payments", "{{paymentId}}"]
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "5. Seller Wallet",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "GET /sellers/me (totals)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const p = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('totalEarnedSatang > 0', () => pm.expect(Number(p.totalEarnedSatang)).to.be.greaterThan(0));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sellers/me",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["sellers", "me"]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "GET /sellers/me/balance (live)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const b = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('returns balance object', () => pm.expect(b.object).to.eql('balance'));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sellers/me/balance",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["sellers", "me", "balance"]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "GET /sellers/me/payouts (live)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sellers/me/payouts",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["sellers", "me", "payouts"]
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "6. Payments — list & detail",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "List my payments (as buyer)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{buyerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["payments"]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "List my payments (as seller)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["payments"]
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "7. Alternate paths (run individually, NOT in collection runner)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Buyer cancels payment (before capture)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{buyerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/cancel",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["payments", "{{paymentId}}", "cancel"]
						},
						"description": "Use this on a Payment that's still in REQUIRES_CAPTURE — i.e. NOT yet captured via confirm-received. Listing returns to AVAILABLE.\n\n⚠️ Only one of `cancel` or `refund` is valid for a given payment, depending on its current state. Don't run both back-to-back in the same Runner pass."
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Seller refunds payment (after capture)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sellerToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"reason\": \"requested_by_customer\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/refund",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["payments", "{{paymentId}}", "refund"]
						},
						"description": "Full refund (omit `amountSatang` for full). Stripe will fire `charge.refunded`, `application_fee.refunded`, `transfer.reversed` webhooks."
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "8. Webhook — simulate payout.paid",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "INFO — run this in your shell",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["health"]
						},
						"description": "Postman can't trigger Stripe events. To verify the `payout.paid` handler increments `totalPaidOutSatang`, run this in a shell:\n\n```bash\nstripe trigger payout.paid \\\n  --stripe-account {{stripeConnectAccountId}}\n```\n\nThen re-run `GET /sellers/me` in folder 5 — `totalPaidOutSatang` should increase.\n\n(In production, this happens automatically T+7 business days after capture.)"
					}
				}
			]
		}
	],
	"event": [
		{
			"listen": "prerequest",
			"script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [""] }
		}
	],
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3003", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "sellerEmail", "value": "1111111111@student.chula.ac.th", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "sellerPassword", "value": "sellerpassword", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "buyerEmail", "value": "2222222222@student.chula.ac.th", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "buyerPassword", "value": "buyerpassword", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "categoryId", "value": "cmp5354ty000fhai0pcbx70qw", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "pickupLocationId", "value": "cmp53dob50014hai00x6horkw", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "sellerToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "buyerToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "sellerUserId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "buyerUserId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "stripeConnectAccountId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
		{ "key": "listingId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
